<Item XName="Note1" UserName="Note1" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;DIV style=&quot;BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 1pt solid; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in; mso-element: para-border-div; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .75pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; TEXT-ALIGN: center; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0in; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .75pt; mso-padding-alt: 0in 0in 1.0pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 18pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;WLAN_11ac_Tx_1ant_80_80MHz&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;This example analyzes the spectrum and&amp;nbsp;Complementary Cumulative Distribution Function (CCDF) of&amp;nbsp;the &lt;SPAN style=&quot;COLOR: black&quot;&gt;802.11ac 80+80 MHz signals.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Users may also save the baseband I/Q data to files or download&amp;nbsp;it to Keysight 89600B VSA software Rev14.0&amp;nbsp;for further analysis. In 89600B Rev14.0, the WLAN 11ac feature is employed to demodulate 11ac signals, and&amp;nbsp;the WLAN 11ac setting for 80MHz+80MHz with single transmitter antenna is provided.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;In the Tx_1ant_80_80MHz design, the parameters defined in the &quot;Parameters&quot; Tab are used to set 11ac 80+80 MHz signal, including the central frequency for each 80MHz segment,&amp;nbsp;MCS and the number of OFDM data symbols in each frame which is determined by the parameters of MCS, CodingType, AggregatedMPDU, NumMPDUPerUser, User0_MPDUDataLength and&amp;nbsp;User0_MPDUMACHeader. The calculated number of data symbols will be displayed in the Errors window.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
